# TIME - Read or set the clock

```text
TIME
TIME /PROVIDER
```

## Read the clock

TIME displays the date and time from the installed clock provider.
/PROVIDER identifies it and reports its read and set capabilities. On
cpmsim load the native clock with RSX LOAD ZPRTC. A Model 4 with a FreHD
clock uses FREHDCLK.

## Set the clock

```text
TIME /SET LL HH HR MN SC
```

The five operands are hexadecimal bytes. LL and HH are the low and high
bytes of the CP/M day count (day 1 is January 1, 1978). HR, MN and SC
are packed decimal digits, so 12 34 56 means 12:34:56. A read-only
provider declines SET.
